1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,000
Hey, we built Curb to help campuses

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,900
figure out which accessibility repairs to fund.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:14,900
In 2022, about one in eight U.S. adults reported
serious difficulty walking or climbing stairs.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,200
We filmed this outside Robertson Hall.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:23,700
When I click Review,
you can see what the analysis flagged.

6
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:30,700
I’ll jump to this patch of broken pavement
and confirm what I see.

7
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:37,900
We’d still need to measure it on site
to know how it affects the route.

8
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,900
Now let’s look at a simulated campus.

9
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,300
Say we’ve got ten grand.

10
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:51,300
Fix the worst spot first
and the whole budget goes to opening Hall.

11
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:57,200
Curb puts five thousand into the ramp
and five into the shared path.

12
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:01,100
That gets us to the Library and Student Center.

13
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,900
Same money, two new destinations instead of one.

14
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:10,900
Here’s the catch.
Take out the ramp and neither route opens.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,900
Put the ramp back and skip the path repair.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,900
Same problem. You need both to get through.

17
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:26,400
If we had twenty grand,
we could do all three repairs.

18
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,900
Then both plans reach the same three new destinations.

19
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:37,550
Curb reached more destinations than condition-first
in fifty-eight synthetic budget cases.

20
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:39,900
The other sixty-two tied.

21
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:44,200
Facilities can take this plan into a budget meeting.

22
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:51,900
Next, we’d walk and measure a real route
with disabled campus users, then get quotes.
